Subject: [PATCH 0068] Breadcrumbs in the IOGraphics callbacks of NMXGPU's framebuffer

Wildcat Lake test start 12 (with 0067): NMXGPUFB::start completed and the start froze with "publish: registerService"
as the last breadcrumb; nothing of that start reached the log. registerService() only queues matching, so the freeze
most likely came from what IOGraphics does with the new framebuffer on its own threads (open, aperture mapping,
display mode, interrupts, power, console).

- xnu/nmx_fb.cpp: a "publish: cb <callback> <argument>" breadcrumb on entry to enableController, isConsoleDevice,
  getApertureRange, getVRAMRange, setDisplayMode, registerForInterruptType, setApertureEnable, setPowerState,
  setAttribute and setAttributeForConnection.
- override/src/nmx_fb_bridge.c: "fb: power" before and after nmx_fb_power's DPMS commit.

Applies on top of 0051-0067.

